//! Camera Raw's exposure transfer, measured (v1.17.0): the table [`super::exposure::Ramp`] reads.
//!
//! Camera Raw rendered a synthetic DNG (camera = linear ProPhoto, its own "Adobe Standard" with an
//! identity tone curve and no tables, so the output IS the transfer) of 291 grey patches, x = 2e-5 to 1
//! of white, at every total exposure E (BaselineExposure + Exposure) in the rows: -5 to +6 every 0.25 EV
//! and nine more beside the kinks at 0, -1, 2 and 4 (+5.25 to +6 through BaselineExposure +1: the slider
//! stops at +5, and BaselineExposure +1 at slider 0 renders exactly as slider +1). 16-bit ProPhoto (pure
//! gamma 1.8), patch means. Each entry is `F(x; E) / (x * 2^E)`, the output over the plain gain, at
//! `log2 x` = [`RAMP_LOG2X`]; rows made monotone in x. Leaving any one row out, its neighbours predict
//! it to 0.66 L* at worst (mean 0.02-0.28 per row).

